# Module conventions

One concern per directory. **Folder name must equal the option name** — `modules/home/fuzzel/`
declares `mine.fuzzel.enable`. Enable it in `systems/common.nix` (NixOS) or `homes/common.nix`
(Home Manager); a module with no toggle there is dead code.

## Skeleton

```nix
{ config, lib, namespace, ... }:
let
  cfg = config.${namespace}.<name>;
in
{
  options.${namespace}.<name>.enable = lib.mkEnableOption "…";

  config = lib.mkIf cfg.enable { … };
}
```

## Package group gating

Use the shared helper, partially applied. Never hand-roll `cfg.enable && cfg.<group>.enable`:

```nix
on = lib.${namespace}.packageGroupOn config.${namespace}.packages;   # then: on "rust"
```

## Splitting a large module

Follow `modules/home/theme/default.nix`: `default.nix` holds `imports` plus the options
declaration, and each submodule owns one tool and repeats the same gate. `modules/home/cli/`
is the other example (`tools.nix`, `broot.nix`, `zellij.nix`, `yazi.nix`).

## The one exception

`modules/home/cli/` declares **no** `options` block and is absent from `homes/common.nix`. It is
gated entirely by `mine.packages.cli.enable`, and every submodule repeats that gate:

```nix
on = lib.${namespace}.packageGroupOn config.${namespace}.packages "cli";
```

Do not "fix" this by adding a `mine.cli.enable` option.

## Other

- Read host facts from `mine.host.*` via `osConfig`. Never branch on `if hostname == …`.
- Take colors from `lib.${namespace}.palette` and its hex converters, not inline literals.
- Packages belong in `modules/home/packages/groups/<group>.nix`, not in feature modules.
